  "model": "x normal, y=delta_star*x+epsilon; noisy mark reliability as declared; fixed population standardization, unit working predictive variance; fit per-star baseline intercepts and pooled nonnegative OLS mark offset on independent synthetic development only",
  "known_rule": "known zero baseline and known common pooled coefficient sqrt(reliability)*mean(delta_star), same evaluation draws as fitted rule",
  "nominal_gain": "mean individual-star oracle gain delta_star^2/2 with perfect markers; heterogeneous pooled or imperfect-marker achieved gain may differ",
  "dependence": "within each star, mark and residual have independent six-block Gaussian effects; serial robustness sets AR(1) .7 across block effects; development/evaluation block series independent",
  "inference": "weighted paired mean, iterated star weight cap .4, star\u00d7six-year CR1 with t_(G-1) one-sided5%; report coverage of conditional expected score gain after fit",
  "scope_limits": [
    "Not X5 or photometry calibration.",
    "No observation count or cadence measured; N is a planning variable.",
    "No extraction, censoring, event eligibility, state-filter learning or variance/standardization estimation is simulated.",
    "Null confirmation rate refers to no-mark-effect generator, not proof of a universal error guarantee."
